	"nodes":[
		{"id":"b30affee541b6f56","type":"text","text":"## **Big question**\nWho is being rude at the tea party? What would good advice sound like?","x":450,"y":-335,"width":600,"height":112,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"ace3ccf5a17cdb3b","type":"text","text":"## **Learning goals**\n**I can:** read dialogue intensively; copy **one sentence** of advice; find **two** rude actions; explain two meanings of *but*; use grammar and health language in writing.","x":450,"y":-195,"width":600,"height":154,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b131bdcfd2bf126e","type":"text","text":"## **Original novel | Chapter VII: A Mad Tea-Party**\n*Lewis Carroll, Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland (1865)*\n\n> ‘Have some wine,’ the March Hare said in an encouraging tone.\n\n> Alice looked all round the table, but there was nothing on it but tea. ‘I don't see any wine,’ she remarked.\n\n> ‘There isn't any,’ said the March Hare.\n\n> ‘Then it wasn't very civil of you to offer it,’ said Alice angrily.\n\n> ‘It wasn't very civil of you to sit down without being invited,’ said the March Hare.\n\n> ‘I didn't know it was your table,’ said Alice; ‘it's laid for a great many more than three.’\n\n> ‘Your hair wants cutting,’ said the Hatter. He had been looking at Alice for some time with great curiosity, and this was his first speech.\n\n> ‘You should learn not to make personal remarks,’ Alice said with some severity; ‘it's very rude.’","x":1140,"y":-335,"width":830,"height":705},
		{"id":"a1e7084cc8139b20","type":"text","text":"## **Context and vocabulary support**\nAlice joins the March Hare and Hatter for tea. They disagree about manners and invitations.\n\n**Mini-glossary outside the original:**\n*civil* = beleefd\n*remark* = opmerking\n*invited* = uitgenodigd\n","x":1140,"y":400,"width":830,"height":213,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"103788ed6f7a8201","type":"text","text":"# **27 November 2026 | 2 VWO**\n### Alice in Wonderland | Lesson 3 of 3","x":-330,"y":-258,"width":650,"height":140,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"f0432fcfae7b1986","x":2367,"y":-30,"width":462,"height":274,"type":"text","text":"## Lets See what You Know \n### Open Kahoot and join the quiz\n## Everyone will have **normal names!** If this is not the case we will stop the kahoot and everyone wil go and make **stepping stones exercises.**\n"}
